- Simplify fresh fork initialization and payout confirmation records
  Initialize fork tables atomically and retain state on same-schema reopen.
  Keep the inherited migration chains and authoritative payment checks.
  Fresh stores are required; earlier experimental fork formats are not converted.
  [#33](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/33)
- Bind Lightning outcomes to the complete payment source
  Keep unrelated payments with the same hash from settling another sender.
  Resume or refund internal payments after an interrupted receive claim.
  Keep unidentified recipients from blocking ready payouts when their shared
  tree can be split safely.
  Require the qualified six-confirmation Core Lightning runtime and preserve
  source-specific incident records for supervised recovery.
  [#33](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/33)
- Recover operator collateral after an offboard forfeit
  Reuse the existing claim path once the collateral is confirmed and mature.
  [#33](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/33)
